1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,204
Forty years. That's how long she painted it.

2
00:00:03,504 --> 00:00:06,916
Every face, every brushstroke — people called it

3
00:00:06,952 --> 00:00:09,657
a miracle. Kings offered fortunes.

4
00:00:09,865 --> 00:00:13,023
Museums literally built wings around it.

5
00:00:13,323 --> 00:00:16,853
And then — one morning — she walked

6
00:00:16,899 --> 00:00:18,292
in with a bucket of white paint.

7
00:00:18,593 --> 00:00:19,870
She covered every inch.

8
00:00:20,381 --> 00:00:22,957
Gone. Just like that.

9
00:00:23,257 --> 00:00:25,695
People thought she'd completely lost her mind.

10
00:00:25,939 --> 00:00:28,599
And honestly? She just smiled.

11
00:00:28,897 --> 00:00:31,242
She said — 'Now it lives only in

12
00:00:31,277 --> 00:00:33,054
the memory of everyone who saw it.

13
00:00:33,228 --> 00:00:34,597
A canvas can burn.

14
00:00:34,715 --> 00:00:37,384
A photograph fades. But what lives inside a

15
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:39,858
person — that's eternal.'

16
00:00:40,158 --> 00:00:41,515
She died a year later.

17
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:44,581
And okay — wait.

18
00:00:45,185 --> 00:00:47,680
Here's where it gets actually wild.

19
00:00:47,981 --> 00:00:50,059
Every single person who saw that mural —

20
00:00:50,106 --> 00:00:51,882
they all remember it differently.

21
00:00:52,207 --> 00:00:55,411
Every one of them saw something completely unique.

22
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:57,417
She didn't destroy her art.

23
00:00:57,661 --> 00:01:01,213
She multiplied it. Into thousands of masterpieces —

24
00:01:01,387 --> 00:01:04,117
one for every soul who looked.

